// The IR pass runner (plan 11 B8): a pass is `{ name, when: fn(&PassCx): bool, run: fn(&PassCx, &Program) }`,
// run in list order after lowering. `validate` (dev builds and tests), `devmode` (dev builds with scripts) and
// `fast` (`--fast`) are entries with a `when`; a new pass is one entry, not a new call site.
//
// Part of module j3c.ir.
// J3: New in plan 11 B8, no Rust file of its own: replaces the hardcoded fast/dev/validate calls in compile.rs
//     and compile/dev.rs.
// J3: `--dump-after=PASS` prints `ir.dump` after that entry and `--time-passes` times each entry with
//     `base/phase`; both come from the runner, so every pass gets them.
// J3: `PassCx` (flags, arena, diags) is built by the driver from its `Session`, since `driver` is below `ir`.
//     The ordered list itself is a constant in `driver.j3`, the only stage that sees both `ir` and `devmode`.
//     This file may not use `backend` or `devmode` (tools/layers.txt).
module j3c.ir;
